{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "סמך לא תחסום למלקות", :translit "samakh lo tachsom lamalkot", :gloss "juxtaposed 'you shall not muzzle' with lashes"} {:he "שרצועה שמלקין בה", :translit "she-ratzu'ah she-malkin bah", :gloss "for the strap with which they lash"} {:he "היא של עגל", :translit "hi shel eigel", :gloss "it is of a calf"} {:he "ידע שור קונהו", :translit "yada shor koneihu", :gloss "an ox knows its owner"} {:he "וזה לא ידע קונו", :translit "ve-zeh lo yada kono", :gloss "and this one does not know its master"} {:he "לפיכך יפרע ברצועה של עגל", :translit "lefichach yifra be-ratzu'ah shel eigel", :gloss "therefore it is paid back with a strap from a calf"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smakhut: the juxtaposition of 'you shall not muzzle an ox' with the laws of lashes (Deut 25:2–3) drives the derashah."}], :frame {:text "Rav Kahana states in the name of Rav that the strap used for lashes must be made from calf-hide, derived from the juxtaposition of 'you shall not muzzle' (Deut 25:4) to the laws of lashes (Deut 25:2–3), with the reasoning: 'An ox knows its owner' (Isaiah 1:3), but this transgressor does not know his Master, therefore he is punished with a calf's hide (Sanhedrin 7a–b).", :sources ["Sanhedrin 7a–b" "Isaiah 1:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smakhut: the juxtaposition of 'you shall not muzzle an ox' with the laws of lashes (Deut 25:2–3) drives the derashah.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:09.826966436Z", :model "glm-5.2"}